    "durationMs": 127736,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end:\n\n- **`server.js`** — Express 5 app: `POST /links` (201 with `clicks: 0`, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 on malformed JSON / invalid url / invalid code, 8-char random code generation with collision retry), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (atomic `UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING url` → 302 with exact `Location`), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`). URLs are stored and returned byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **Persistence** — `pg` Pool reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment; a `migrate.js` runner applies pending SQL migrations from `migrations/` inside transactions. Click counts and links survive restarts (verified: clicks went 0 → 2 → restart → 3).\n- **`start.sh`** — applies migrations then `exec node server.js` in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; re-runs are idempotent.\n- **Validation rules tested** — rel/ftp/no-host URLs, non-string url, short/long/space codes, malformed JSON, unknown routes, encoded path codes all return the right status with an `error` field.\n- `pg` was installed now (not in start.sh), README documents startup, and I left the database pristine with no background processes running."
